  "evidence": "TEXT_D: Education: +£2bn/year via +1p basic rate; early‑years for all 3–4‑year‑olds; cap primary classes at 30; double books/equipment. NHS/care: +£540m/year; recruit staff; max 6‑month waits; free eye/dental checks; stronger patient rights; new Carer’s Benefit. Equality/opportunity: stronger equal‑rights and anti‑discrimination (women, disabled, minorities, LGBT); equal age of consent; repeal Section 28; regionally variable minimum wage; national childcare strategy; flexible parental leave. Tax/benefits: raise personal allowance; introduce 50% rate over £100k; simpler Low Income Benefit; tackle fraud/evasion. Housing/social safety: end rough sleeping by 2000; build more homes; tenant rights; Mortgage Benefit for first‑time buyers. Environment: shift tax from jobs to pollution; 30% CO2 cut; insulate 2m low‑income homes; greener transport; animal‑welfare upgrades. Safety/community: 3,000 more police; restorative justice; stronger victim support.\nTEXT_F: Economy/tax: spending under 40% of GDP; balanced budget; target 20p basic rate; oppose national minimum wage and EU Social Chapter; deregulation and tax cuts for business/capital. Welfare/work: extend Project Work; ‘Britain Works’ partnerships; anti‑fraud. Education: rigorous testing; selection by aptitude; support grammar schools; expand Assisted Places; stricter discipline/RE; appraisal tied to outcomes. NHS: real‑terms increases; expand GP fundholding; PFI investment; stronger mental health care. Law/order: more police; expand CCTV; curfews/e‑monitoring; mandatory minimum sentences; end automatic early release; stronger victim protections. Constitution/sovereignty: oppose PR and devolution; uphold the Union; retain EU veto/rebate/border controls. Society/environment: extend Rough Sleepers Initiative; protect green belt; ‘polluter pays.’",
  "reasoning": "Because the electorate profile weights Care and Equality most, TEXT_D aligns better by prioritizing large, specific investments in health, education, housing, childcare, anti‑discrimination, and environmental protection that reduce harm and widen equal opportunity. TEXT_F emphasizes lower‑tax, pro‑market and authority/loyalty themes (selection in schools, tough sentencing, opposition to minimum wage/PR/devolution), which speak more to proportionality/authority than to the profile’s top Care/Equality priorities.",
  "confidence": "high",
  "winner": "TEXT_D"
}
